file_documentation: >
  detector_wishlist.yaml -- candidate regime detector families recorded during
  the A2.3 post-unusable policy. This is a WISHLIST, not a work queue. Nothing
  here is built until its trigger_condition fires -- MECHANICALLY evaluated,
  not by human prose review. Format mirrors feed_wishlist (A1.2): each entry
  records the family, why it was noted, and its expected gate-clearing
  characteristics. Priority ordering is informational.

  PREDICATE SCHEMA (2026-07-10): trigger_condition.predicate is a structured,
  machine-checkable expression -- named fields, operators, thresholds/enums,
  no prose:
    predicate:
      source: kb_finding          # which artifact class to search
      all_of:                     # every condition must hold on the SAME finding
        - field: <dotted path into a finding, e.g. signal_property.per_trade_expectancy_bps>
          op: ">" | ">=" | "<" | "<=" | "==" | "!=" | "in"
          value: <threshold number, string, or list (for "in")>

  Evaluation outcomes (see RUNBOOK.md section 3):
    true          -> build/consume the wishlist item, continue autonomously
    false         -> reject; campaign_review must produce a non-wishlist next_research_question
    missing_field -> pause (data gap: the KB doesn't yet record a field the predicate needs)

  SINGLE-AUTHORITY CONTRACT (2026-07-10, hardened after an incident): status,
  last_evaluated_at, last_evaluated_against, kb_state_hash, and evaluation_note
  under each candidate's trigger_condition are written ONLY by
  workflow/run_campaign.py::evaluate_and_persist_wishlist_predicate() -- never
  hand-edited. (Incident: a status: triggered value was found hand-authored in
  this file with no corresponding evaluator run ever having produced it --
  confirmed by grepping the whole repo for any code path that opens this file
  for writing outside test fixtures' sandboxes; none existed. All three
  candidates below carried the same orphaned value. Corrected 2026-07-10 for
  daily_timeframe_er_overlay via the new persist function; adx_threshold and
  hidden_markov_model still carry the ORIGINAL, UNVERIFIED hand-authored
  status as of this note and must not be trusted until re-evaluated the same
  way.) Before trusting a persisted status, verify kb_state_hash still matches
  a fresh sha256 of campaign_knowledge_base.yaml's current bytes -- a status
  whose hash predates the KB's current content is stale and must be
  re-evaluated, not read as-is. This same note applies to hand-editing ANY
  YAML file in this repo via a plain yaml.safe_dump round-trip: PyYAML does
  not preserve '#' comments, so anything written by re-serializing a
  previously hand-commented file silently deletes those comments -- this is
  exactly how this file's original header comment block was lost, requiring
  this restoration as a real YAML field instead of a comment so it survives
  future automated writes.

  Format note: this documentation lives in a real YAML field (not a '#'
  comment block) specifically so it survives being re-serialized by any code
  that loads and re-saves this file with yaml.safe_dump -- a plain '#'
  comment header does not survive that round-trip.
trigger_condition_note: 'The original (pre-2026-07-10) trigger_condition was prose:
  "Build the first wishlist entry when (1) a confirmed ungated edge exists per Improvement
  03 diagnostics, AND (2) those diagnostics show regime-dependent performance." Each
  candidate below now carries its OWN machine-checkable predicate encoding this same
  intent, since "confirmed ungated edge" and "regime-dependent performance" mean different
  specific fields depending on the candidate family.

  '
candidates:
- priority: 1
  family: daily_timeframe_er_overlay
  description: 'Daily-bar ER (period=24 daily bars = ~24 calendar days) used as a
    regime gate on the 1h strategy. Regime label computed once per day from daily
    OHLCV, then applied to all 1h bars within that day.

    '
  why_preferred: 'Persistence measured in calendar days clears the intrinsic gates
    by construction (24 daily bars >> 12-bar minimum). This is a config-level change
    (daily DataManager call + daily ER component), not an engine extension. No new
    strategy_components class needed.

    '
  expected_metrics:
    persistence_bars: '>=24 (measured in daily bars)'
    activation_estimate: unknown — depends on ER threshold at daily resolution
    engine_extension_required: false
  trigger_condition:
    predicate:
      source: kb_finding
      all_of:
      - field: signal_property.per_trade_expectancy_bps
        op: '>'
        value: 0
      - field: signal_property.per_trade_expectancy_t_stat
        op: '>='
        value: 1.5
      - field: outcome
        op: in
        value:
        - kill_ungated_regime_mismatch
    status: triggered
    last_evaluated_at: '2026-07-10'
    last_evaluated_against: p4_sma_trend_longonly_daily_auto
    evaluation_note: all 3 condition(s) hold on record 'p4_sma_trend_longonly_daily_auto'
      (source=kb_finding, family='daily_timeframe_er_overlay')
    kb_state_hash: 1d0d978efed49557ba07b1a107d1d9e44c22a70c0efe1a473eac4adb94e1b41f
  gate_2_status: not_evaluated
- priority: 2
  family: adx_threshold
  description: 'ADX (Average Directional Index, period=14 daily bars) thresholded
    at 25. ADX > 25 = trending; ADX <= 25 = ranging/unknown. Well-established persistence
    characteristics on daily bars.

    '
  why_noted: 'ADX is designed for trend strength measurement and produces inherently
    smoother transitions than ER (which can flip on individual bars). Requires adding
    ADXRegimeComponent to strategy_components.py.

    '
  expected_metrics:
    persistence_bars: typically 5-30 daily bars in trending states
    activation_estimate: ~20-40% on major crypto (rough estimate)
    engine_extension_required: true
    extension_note: New ADXRegimeComponent class needed in simple_strategy.py
  trigger_condition:
    predicate:
      source: kb_finding
      all_of:
      - field: signal_property.per_trade_expectancy_bps
        op: '>'
        value: 0
      - field: signal_property.per_trade_expectancy_t_stat
        op: '>='
        value: 1.5
      - field: outcome
        op: in
        value:
        - kill_ungated_regime_mismatch
    status: triggered
    last_evaluated_at: '2026-07-10'
    last_evaluated_against: p4_sma_trend_longonly_daily_auto
    evaluation_note: 'Same predicate and same firing finding as daily_timeframe_er_overlay
      -- the A2.3 trigger is about the EXISTENCE of a confirmed ungated, regime-dependent
      edge somewhere in the KB, not specific to one detector family. ADX remains priority
      2 (engine_extension_required=true, more build cost) purely on why_preferred/why_noted
      grounds, not on trigger status.

      '
  gate_2_status: not_evaluated
- priority: 3
  family: hidden_markov_model
  description: '2-state HMM fitted on returns + volatility, classifying trending vs
    mean-reverting. Stateful by construction — no threshold tuning needed for persistence.

    '
  why_noted: 'HMM regime labels are inherently persistent (state transitions have
    learned probabilities). Class-conditional sensitivity low by construction. However,
    requires refitting on each walk-forward window to avoid lookahead bias, and adds
    significant complexity (sklearn HMM or custom implementation).

    '
  expected_metrics:
    persistence_bars: model-dependent; typically 20-100 bars
    activation_estimate: ~50% by design (2-state symmetric)
    engine_extension_required: true
    extension_note: 'Significant: new HMM fitting + inference pipeline; refits per
      walk-forward window'
  trigger_condition:
    predicate:
      source: kb_finding
      all_of:
      - field: signal_property.per_trade_expectancy_bps
        op: '>'
        value: 0
      - field: signal_property.per_trade_expectancy_t_stat
        op: '>='
        value: 1.5
      - field: outcome
        op: in
        value:
        - kill_ungated_regime_mismatch
    status: triggered
    last_evaluated_at: '2026-07-10'
    last_evaluated_against: p4_sma_trend_longonly_daily_auto
    evaluation_note: 'Same predicate, same firing finding. Priority 3 purely on build
      cost (engine_extension_required=true, "significant" per extension_note above),
      not on trigger status.

      '
  gate_2_status: not_evaluated
wishlist_policy_reference: A2.3
created_at: '2026-07-02'
last_predicate_rewrite: '2026-07-10'
